From 1b9247b139af041096bebee79a017b519da622ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:29:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/58] serve: --batch runs an image request alone; a dead
 encoder fails only image requests

The engine keeps one M-RoPE table per device for all batch slots (previous commit), so an image request must not share
the batch.  generate_batched hands a request with embeddings to _generate_alone: it queues behind earlier image
requests (image_line), new requests stand back from its arrival (not counted as waiting, so a read that gave way
still gets the control lines - no deadlock), the slots decode to their end, then it takes the control lines with
every slot free and runs GENI on the solo path to its DONE (never promoted into a slot).
- STRATA_IMAGE_WAIT_S (120): an image that waited longer for the slots gives up with a 503 the client can retry
  (ImageWaitTimeout, a GpuBusy), and the text held behind it goes on.
- An engine refusal ("ERR vision: ...", a slot the server had already freed) waits for the slots again (up to 3 tries)
  instead of failing.
- A dead or unstartable vision encoder no longer fails text-only requests (load(vision=False) for generation; the
  encoder is started for image requests and tool pictures only).
Text-only traffic sends the same lines as before.  test_image_alone.py: 13 tests (gate, deadlock case, order, cancel,
engine death, restart, orphan flag, timeout, refusal retry, over HTTP with the fake engine).

Measured on 4x RTX 3090 (k5 engine, CPU encoder, T16-143-prod262r + --vision): 15/15 image checks, 16 text users +
images for 90 s: 491 tok/s text, every image answered correctly in 4.8-11.3 s.

